{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And they will listen to your voice.</b> Rashi: Jacob said to them, 'Elohim will surely visit you.' But this is difficult, for this verse is not about Jacob." "<b>Has happened upon us.</b> On our account, as in 'for your sake I have borne humiliation' (Psalms 69:8)." "<b>A journey of three days.</b> And so they did, as it is written 'and they camped on the second day at Etham, at the edge of the wilderness.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Chizkuni cites Rashi's interpretation then rejects it with the marker חז״ק (חזק קשה, 'this is difficult'), noting the verse Rashi cites (Gen 50:24) is spoken by Jacob in a different context, not here in Exodus."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:02.522877788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}